abstract:
Drseed_qa_dataset.json is a Chinese Multi-hop Question Answering (QA) dataset tailored for crop breeding knowledge. It is designed for evaluating Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)-based knowledge service systems in the breeding domain. The data uses variety approval and promotion documents as its knowledge source and is hierarchically constructed by hop counts (hops). Each sample provides all standard supporting paragraphs required to answer the question, requiring cross-paragraph information aggregation. The corpus covers five major crop categories: maize, rice, wheat, soybean, and cotton. The content encompasses core breeding business information including variety origin & pedigree, agronomic traits, disease resistance & quality, yield performance, approval & suitable planting regions, and cultivation techniques. The questions mainly focus on numerical attribute queries, listing/aggregation, comparisons, and calculations. Evaluation Positioning The dataset provides standard supporting paragraphs and reference answers for each question, supporting two evaluation modes for RAG knowledge service systems: End-to-End QA Evaluation: Input the question into the complete system (self-built breeding knowledge base retrieval + generation). Use answer to evaluate the accuracy of the final output, and use paragraph titles in paragraphs as ground truth to verify whether retrieved knowledge chunks match. Generation and Reasoning Capacity Evaluation: Directly feed paragraphs as the retrieved context to the generation model. This isolates the retrieval phase to independently assess model performance in multi-paragraph aggregation, numerical comparison, and arithmetic reasoning based on the provided breeding materials. Reporting results grouped by 1/2/3/4-hop reveals system performance degradation as aggregation depth increases. Files File Count Size Description Drseed_qa_dataset.json 800 ≈1.7 MB Full dataset, UTF-8 encoded JSON array, all used for test Data Format The top level is a JSON array where each element represents a single QA sample: { "id": "2hop__71_183", "paragraphs": [ { "idx": 0, "title": "Dongnong 264 · Traits", "paragraph_text": "Traits of Dongnong 264: Northern East-China Medium-Early Spring Maize Zone, emergence to maturity 126.5 days... crude fat 4.01%..." }, { "idx": 1, "title": "Dadihong 99 · Traits", "paragraph_text": "Traits of Dadihong 99: Semi-compact plant type... crude fat 4.8%..." } ], "question": "Comparing Dongnong 264 and Dadihong 99, which variety has a higher crude fat content?", "answer": "Dadihong 99 is higher, at 4.8%, while Dongnong 264 is 4.01%." } Field Descriptions Field Type Description id string Format: {n}hop__{p1}_{p2}_…_{pn}. The prefix indicates the hop count, and after __ are the global paragraph IDs in the corpus used for this sample, sorted in ascending order and separated by underscores. The same ID consistently corresponds to the same paragraph across the dataset. paragraphs list List of supporting paragraphs, with length strictly equal to the hop count n. All paragraphs are supporting paragraphs without any distractors. paragraphs[].idx int Local index of the paragraph within this sample, ranging from 0 … n-1. paragraphs[].title string Paragraph title, formatted as Variety Name · Section Name (using · as separator). paragraphs[].paragraph_text string Plain Chinese text body containing dense numerical values and units. question string Chinese question that requires combining all supporting paragraphs to answer. answer string Reference answer, provided as a complete Chinese sentence (including entity names, numerical values, and units) rather than an extractive text span. The dataset contains no positive/negative paragraph labels, question decomposition annotations, answer aliases, or answerability labels. All samples are answerable. Data Statistics Overall Scale Metric Value Total QA Pairs 800 Varieties Covered 47 Avg. Paragraph Reuse 12.0 (Median 5.5, Max 64) Paragraph Length (Chars) Min 28 / Median 243 / Max 678 Question Length (Chars) Min 12 / Median 34 / Max 63 Answer Length (Chars) Min 10 / Median 29 / Max 90 id and question are completely unique with no duplicates. Hop Distribution Hop Count Quantity Ratio 1-hop 80 10% 2-hop 160 20% 3-hop 400 50% 4-hop 160 20% Reasoning Structure Multi-hop samples are categorized into two types based on whether supporting paragraphs belong to the same variety: Hop Count Cross-Variety (Different Varieties per Paragraph) Same-Variety Cross-Section Hybrid 2-hop 42 118 0 3-hop 256 99 45 4-hop 90 20 50 Cross-Variety samples align and compare the same attribute across different varieties. Same-Variety Cross-Section samples require aggregating information scattered across different sections (e.g., Traits / Yield Performance / Cultivation Techniques) for a single variety. Question Types Automatically classified by question keywords (Priority order: Numerical Calculation > Comparison/Extremum > List Aggregation > Fact Retrieval): Hop Count Fact Retrieval List Aggregation Comparison/Extremum Numerical Calculation Total 1-hop 60 6 8 6 80 2-hop 60 14 33 53 160 3-hop 6 90 192 112 400 4-hop 0 35 64 61 160 Total 126 145 297 232 800 Fact Retrieval: Directly extracts a single attribute value (e.g., "What is the number of bolls per plant for Zhongmian 113?"). List Aggregation: Lists the same attribute across multiple entities in parallel (e.g., "What are the ear heights for Dongnong 264, Liangyu 968, Liangdan 24, and Tianyu 108?"). Comparison/Extremum: Cross-entity comparison or extreme value search (e.g., "Among MY73, Kangyunuowu, and Woyu 3, which variety had the lowest average yield per mu in two-year regional trials?"). Numerical Calculation: Involves arithmetic operations such as subtraction, addition, or averaging. Section Distribution Distribution of paragraphs by section type: Section Paragraph Count Content Basic Information 46 Structured key-value strings: Crop Category, Index Category, Approval Number, Variety Name, Applicant, Breeder, Variety Source, etc. Traits 44 Plant type, growth period, plant height, ear height, 100-grain weight, disease resistance, quality indices, etc. Yield Performance 40 Yield per mu and yield increase percentage in regional trials and production trials. Approval & Suitable Regions 31 Approval conclusion and suitable cultivation regions. Cultivation Techniques 22 Sowing date, planting density, fertilization, pest and disease control. Resistance & Quality 3 Disease resistance evaluation and quality analysis. Crop Distribution Statistics based on the "Crop Category" field in the Basic Information section: Crop Variety Count Rice 11 Wheat 10 Maize 9 Soybean 9 Cotton 8 Dataset Characteristics Core difficulty lies in cross-paragraph numerical aggregation and comparison: All provided paragraphs are relevant to the answer without distractor elements. This design reflects that the dataset is specifically intended to evaluate RAG system QA performance, where actual inputs to the system come from user knowledge bases. Complete sentence answers: Answers contain entity names, numerical values, and units (e.g., "Dadihong 99 is higher, at 4.8%, while Dongnong 264 is 4.01%."), aligning with real-world user-facing outputs of knowledge service systems rather than contiguous text spans from source documents. Paragraph titles serve as ground truth for retrieval evaluation: The standardized format Variety Name · Section Name enables direct one-to-one checking between retrieved knowledge chunks and gold supporting paragraphs. Shared paragraphs between 1-hop and multi-hop samples: The 80 single-hop samples share knowledge sources with multi-hop samples, enabling isolated evaluation between single-point information extraction and cross-paragraph aggregation abilities. Dense numerical metrics: Breeding indicators and units (cm, g, kg/mu, %, cN/tex, g/L, etc.) appear frequently in text bodies and answers, placing high demands on numerical faithfulness of generation models. Loading Code import json from collections import Counter with open("seed_qa_dataset.json", encoding="utf-8") as f: data = json.load(f) print(len(data)) # 800 print(Counter(r["id"].split("__")[0] for r in data)) # Hop distribution Construct context and prompt for a single sample: r = data[0] context = "

".join(f"【{p['title']}】{p['paragraph_text']}" for p in r["paragraphs"]) prompt = f"Answer the question based on the following material.

{context}

Question: {r['question']}
Answer:" Filter subsets by hop count or crop variety: # Filter by hop count four_hop = [r for r in data if r["id"].startswith("4hop__")] # Filter by variety (prefix before separator in title) def varieties_of(record): return {p["title"].split("·")[0] for p in record["paragraphs"]} maize = [r for r in data if "Dongnong 264" in varieties_of(r)] Evaluation Methods 1. Answer Quality Since reference answers are complete Chinese sentences rather than exact text spans, strict Exact Match leads to high false-negative rates. The following methods are recommended: 1. Numerical / Entity Match (Recommended) Extract numerical values (with units) and variety names from predictions and reference answers, then compute precision, recall, and F1 across the sets. import re NUM = re.compile(r"\d+(?:\.\d+)?\s*(?:%|厘米|毫米|米|克|千克|公斤|天|层|个|行|片|cN/tex|克/升)?") def numbers(text): return {m.group().replace(" ", "") for m in NUM.finditer(text)} def numeric_f1(pred, gold): p, g = numbers(pred), numbers(gold) if not p or not g: return 0.0 inter = len(p & g) prec, rec = inter / len(p), inter / len(g) return 0.0 if inter == 0 else 2 * prec * rec / (prec + rec) 2. Charac

